                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_25\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit adds a single line, `filesFromThisSite.clear();`, at the start of\nXMLFileReader.read(), right after `this.updateSite = updateSite;` is set. This\nensures the `filesFromThisSite` set only ever contains files belonging to the\nupdate site currently being parsed.\n\nSearching the candidates for `filesFromThisSite` shows it only appears in\ncandidate_25, candidate_26, and candidate_27:\n\n- candidate_27 is actually the fix commit itself (its diff is byte-for-byte\n  identical to fix_commit_diff.txt), so it cannot be the bug-introducing commit.\n- candidate_26 only changes `warnings.append(...)` calls to `files.log.warn(...)`\n  for logging shadowed-file warnings; it does not touch the `filesFromThisSite`\n  bookkeeping logic.\n- candidate_25 is the commit that FIRST introduces the `filesFromThisSite` field\n  (`protected Set<FileObject> filesFromThisSite = new HashSet<FileObject>();`)\n  and rewrites the file-merging logic in `read()` to use\n  `filesFromThisSite.contains(file)` instead of the previous\n  `updateSite.equals(file.updateSite)` check to decide whether a file being\n  parsed belongs to the same update site as an already-known file (needed to\n  correctly detect shadowing between update sites).\n\nHowever, candidate_25 never clears `filesFromThisSite` between successive calls\nto `read()` (which is called once per update site). Since `XMLFileReader` is\nreused across multiple update-site reads, `filesFromThisSite` accumulates\nentries from all previously-read sites. This means the `contains(file)` check\nused to decide \"is this file already known from the site I'm currently\nparsing?\" would incorrectly return true for files from OTHER update sites too,\ncausing the code to take the \"same site, just update the object\" branch instead\nof the shadowing/override branch \u2014 effectively preventing any update site's\nfiles from properly shadowing (overriding) files from a different update site,\nexactly the symptom described in the fix commit message (\"the bug would\nprevent any shadowing\").\n\nThe fix simply adds the missing `filesFromThisSite.clear()` call, which\nrestores correct per-site scoping of the set introduced in candidate_25. Since\ncandidate_25 is the commit that introduced this stateful field and the logic\ndepending on it (without the necessary reset), it is the bug-introducing\ncommit.\n"
                }
              }
            ]
